From 364e35f1e0e2151f2b882a84135ddc57b2497e18 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dev <dev@local>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 21:37:33 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 20/97] feat(ponder): let the touch button be dragged, and
 remember where

The button is a permanent floating element over every page, and on a phone the
right-hand edge is exactly where each page puts its own buttons - the collection
page's list/search pair, the player's panel handle. Pinned to one corner it is
guaranteed to sit on top of something, and which something depends on the page,
which the component itself cannot predict.

So the position becomes the user's: drag it once and it stays there. Stored in
viewport coordinates (utils/ponder/ponderTouchButtonPosition owns the clamp, the
parse and the serialize), re-clamped on every viewport change so a spot dropped
in portrait cannot land off-screen in landscape.

Dragging writes left/top straight to the node and keeps the live coordinate in a
ref: a pointermove routed through React state would re-render PonderHost once per
frame, which is the one thing this tree must not do while the visualizer is
running (skills/frontend-runtime-guardrails). The store is written once, on drop.

The reveal hotspot follows the button instead of staying pinned to the top-right
corner - a 96px touch target centred on wherever it was dropped, because the old
corner no longer has anything to press. A drag feeds the existing
suppress-next-click flag, so letting go of the button does not open the ponder
session; and the 4s hide timer no longer fires out from under a finger that is
still holding it.

Moved from `right-5 top-5` to inline left/top for the same reason the drag needs
it: a position expressed as "distance from the right edge" says nothing about a
coordinate that is being dragged.
